{"uid":"sn1.18","title":"Conscience","reference":"Saṁyutta Nikāya 1.18","blocks":[{"kind":"verse","lines":["“Can a person constrained by conscience","be found in the world,","who is cognizant of blame,","like a fine horse of the whip?”","“Few are those constrained by conscience,","who live always mindful.","Having reached the end of suffering,","smoothly they walk in the rough.”"]}]}
